Title: CROWN OF IRON: THE TREATY OF 1588
Genre: Historical Drama
Recommended Style: Oscar-Level Prestige Cinema & Golden Age Painted Realism

INT. WINCHESTER CASTLE - GREAT HALL - NIGHT
[STYLE: Oscar-Level Prestige Cinema | LIGHTING: Natural Candelabra Chiaroscuro]

Thick wax candles flicker against cold granite masonry. A fire crackles in the great hearth, illuminating tapestries of medieval conquest.

LORD CHANCELLOR BURGHLEY (60s, ermine-lined velvet robes, weathered statesman) unrolls a wax-sealed treaty before QUEEN ELIZABETH (50s, imperial posture, embroidered pearl bodice).

BURGHLEY
If you sign this covenant with the Spanish envoys, Madame, you purchase ten years of peace for England.

ELIZABETH
(her gaze piercing the darkness)
Peace purchased with Spanish gold is merely a lease on our own executions, William. Call the fleet commanders. We fight at gravelines.
